I'm making a snake game in C. I'm stuck at the point where I want to make the snake move using arrow keys. I tried to use this code:
```
if (xpos + 20 > 800) xpos = 0;
else if (ypos + 20 > 600) ypos = 0;
else if (xpos + 20 < 0) xpos = 800;
else if (ypos + 20 < 0) ypos = 600;
```
It works fine, but when I move the snake to the right, it is not smooth, it just goes to the next square, and I want it to be smooth, like when you move it from right to left it should move to the left square but smoothly, not just go to the next square. How can I do that?

### 2 answers

There are several ways to achieve this. I'll give you a couple:

  1. Instead of using a single image for your snake, use several images, one for each direction, and display them one after the other when the snake moves. So you have a left, right, up, and down image. Each time you need to move the snake, you move the body, then update the image. The speed of the snake will depend on how many frames you display before changing the image.
  2. A more advanced version of the above is to use a sprite sheet. This is where you have all the images for your snake in one image, with each image next to each other. You then move the snake body, then update the position of the sprite in the sprite sheet so the correct image is displayed.

Both of these methods will allow you to make your snake move smoothly.

