```python
def common_elements(arr1, arr2):
    common = []
    for i in arr1:
        for j in arr2:
            if i == j:
                common.append(i)
    return common
```
Explanation:
The above implementation uses two for loops to iterate through the elements of both arrays and compares each element. If an element is found in both arrays, it is added to the common array. The time complexity of this solution is O(n^2) where n is the length of the longer array.
